            "text": "a. Impact of Fertilizers: The toxic chemicals found in fertilizers can be absorbed into the plants and enter the food chain via vegetables and cereals, although the biggest health risk is when the chemicals seep into the ground water which is then extracted for drinking water. This water can contain high levels of nitrates and nitrites which can cause blue-baby syndrome (methemoglobinemia). Mercury, lead, cadmium and uranium are some of the toxic heavy metals that have been found in fertilizers and can cause disturbances of the kidneys, lungs and liver. (Fig 2.17: Adding fertilizers do increase the overall yield but it also have negative impacts on the environment.)",
