            "text": "Over the last hundred years there has been a sharp rise in population. This problem is more serious in the developing world as compared to the developed world. Consistent rise in the population is posing serious challenges to the developing world. Unfortunately, due to bad governance and lack of strong economic growth, people living in these areas are suffering from poverty, hunger, and disease. Any area has a limited carrying capacity in terms of resources and space. Once that carrying capacity is taken over by over population then slowly and gradually degradation takes its root. The environment of such an area gives a clear picture of how overpopulation devastates and affects the lives of the people living in such areas. In the following section we will see how overpopulation has its impacts on the environment.",
