            "text": "After obtaining preliminary information, you would have realized the value and importance of energy in modern society. You may have also noticed that conventional sources of energy are limited. Exploitation of non-conventional energy sources is still in the initial stages of research and development. The fuel that burns in factories and transport vehicles or performs other activities is mainly obtained from underground deposits in the form of coal, oil, natural gas and other similar raw forms. These deposits are rapidly decreasing. The rapid growth in population increases the pressure on the use of resources. The excessive and unwise use of resources affects the environment. After all, one day all the resources of energy will be exhausted. It is therefore highly important for us to avoid wastage of energy and conserve energy by taking suitable steps at our homes, schools, industries and offices etc.",
